### Tier 2: Essential Patching (15 minutes)
**Upgrade Spring Cloud Gateway to patched version immediately**

Patched versions:
- **3.1.x**: Must upgrade to 3.1.1+
- **3.0.x**: Must upgrade to 3.0.7+
- **2.2.x and older**: Update entire Spring Cloud version (consider 2.4.x+ LTS)

```xml
<!-- pom.xml -->
<properties>
  <!-- CURRENT (VULNERABLE) -->
  <!-- <spring-cloud.version>2021.0.5</spring-cloud.version> --> <!-- Includes Gateway 3.0.5 -->

  <!-- PATCHED (REQUIRED) -->
  <spring-cloud.version>2022.0.1</spring-cloud.version>  <!-- Includes Gateway 3.1.1+ -->
</properties>

<dependencyManagement>
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-cloud-dependencies</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-cloud.version}</version>
      <type>pom</type>
      <scope>import</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
</dependencyManagement>

<dependencies>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-gateway</artifactId>
    <!-- Version will be resolved from dependencyManagement -->
  </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

**Verify patched version in use:**

```bash
mvn dependency:tree | grep spring-cloud-gateway
# Should show: org.springframework.cloud:spring-cloud-gateway:jar:3.1.1

# After upgrade and deployment, verify version at runtime:
curl http://your-gateway:8080/actuator/health/livenessState
# The response headers and gateway logs should indicate new version
```

**CRITICAL: Test in staging environment first**
- Spring Cloud 2022.0.x has some breaking changes from 2021.0.x
- Test all custom filters, route configurations, and downstream services
- Verify performance (version upgrades may affect latency)
- Run full integration test suite

