## Testing

```java
@SpringBootTest
public class GatewaySecurityTests {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Test
    public void testSpELInjectionBlocked() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/actuator/gateway/routes/test")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content("{\"filters\":[{\"args\":{\"value\":\"#{T(java.lang.Runtime)...\"}}]}")
            .with(httpBasic("admin", "password")))
            .andExpect(status().isForbidden());
    }

    @Test
    public void testActuatorRequiresAuth() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(get("/actuator/gateway/routes"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
    }

    @Test
    public void testRefreshRequiresAuth() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/actuator/gateway/refresh"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
    }

    @Test
    public void testAuthenticatedAccessAllowed() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(get("/actuator/gateway/routes")
            .with(httpBasic("gateway-admin", "securePassword")))
            .andExpect(status().isOk());
    }
}
```

## Incident Response

If you suspect your gateway was compromised:

```bash
# 1. IMMEDIATELY: Check for suspicious routes
http://your-gateway:8080/actuator/gateway/routes | grep -v "expected-route"

# 2. Check system logs for reverse shell attempts
sudo tail -f /var/log/auth.log | grep -i "bash\|nc\|telnet"

# 3. Check network connections from gateway process
sudo netstat -antp | grep java

# 4. Isolate gateway from network
sudo iptables -A OUTPUT -j DROP  # Block all outbound until investigation complete

# 5. Preserve evidence and rebuild from clean image
sudo docker pull myregistry/spring-cloud-gateway:3.1.1-patched
sudo docker run --rm -v /root/.docker/config.json:/root/.docker/config.json...

# 6. Notify stakeholders and begin forensics
# Contact legal, compliance, affected customers per breach notification requirements
```

